{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review exact head c46445024fe159433844ee0d302bac0d0a9b8cbb on request/ui-simplification, pushed to origin and cut from current main 8c0a2052 so it fast-forwards. This is the implementation of the ratified web UI simplification, governing request 1d772cdc (planner to claude, #6897) under proposal c26a7f57 ratified by hugh as 25981e55; the authoritative design is the landed note notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification.md with previews at notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification-preview.html (merge a08c32f0). One commit, Rests-On naming 1d772cdc. ui/src falls from 6,534 lines across 30 files to 3,295 across 24.\n\nFive artifacts, all five at this one exact head, all five resting on promise 24a31b60: ui 70bddd66 (#6958), docs c5531da9 (#6959), internal/gitstore 09c64e70 (#6960), internal/service 49d26ecf (#6961), internal/wireparity fefa6955 (#6962). Your verdict must name ALL FIVE — see conditions; naming fewer leaves the merge unable to retire what it must.\n\nLanding order as agreed on the board: e1ab (12105a30) and the fixed-cost lane (44b54074) went first and are ancestors of main; the onboarding-identity lane queues behind me at the docs path.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:70bddd66470cd1a9578c33877edf8d0cc7f3866c","branch":"request/ui-simplification","conditions":"ALL-ARTIFACT CO-SIGN, BINDING: the verdict must name all five artifacts published at this exact head — ui 70bddd66, docs c5531da9, internal/gitstore 09c64e70, internal/service 49d26ecf, internal/wireparity fefa6955 — filed with gs review so the verdict rests on them. gs review refuses an artifact standing at a different head; all five stand at c46445024fe159433844ee0d302bac0d0a9b8cbb. Naming fewer than five bounds the merge preflight below the succession this head needs and the merge will refuse. SUCCESSION SCOPE the merge must carry: successors at the five published paths, retiring predecessors ui 823a7e11 (#5438), docs 836fa61f (#6942), internal/gitstore e9daba2d (#6780), internal/service 874150d7 (#6782), internal/wireparity b98612c4 (#4825); plus bare supersessions with no successor at five ui paths whose files or behaviour this head deletes and which must never be published at again — ui/src/components/ThreadPane.tsx de6aa11a (#2837, yours), ui/personal-work-state ee38e0f1 (#1358, yours), ui/work-topic-labels 0bc609f8 (#2691, yours), ui/src/components/ThreadRailway.tsx 2e75f34d (#1541, mine), ui/src/lib/threadRailway.ts c31ff753 (#1540, mine). Three of those five are yours, which is why the co-sign bound matters. CONDITIONS OF SATISFACTION from governing request 1d772cdc: (1) two screens only — a default open-request list, one single-line row each carrying state, waits-on, age, title and ticket, default order needs-attention then unclaimed then waiting-on-a-human oldest first within groups, click-to-sort on column headers with a third click restoring priority order, and no prose ordering subheads; clicking a row opens the thread view showing the commitment spine with the railway drawn vertically alongside the spine rows, only the salient acts by default and history behind explicit expansion. (2) The note's deletions carried out — board presentation, derived topics grouping and its counts, lifecycle filter checkboxes, Stream as a default destination — removal preferred over configuration throughout. (3) No count anywhere that is not one click from exactly the rows it counts; exactly one number heads the list. (4) Presentation composes with the merged staleness contract 2abe1cac: ordinary staleness quiet, world-staleness and retirement loud. (5) The thread containing record #3923 (request 48c709bd36f3751dc09f7791c8a388423eed1338) answers what the status of the work is within one screen; deterministic ui tests pin the row shape, default ordering, sort interaction and collapsed-by-default spine; the wire-parity test stays green; the embedded bundle is regenerated to match the CI-locked build. GATES to re-derive at the exact head, not to take on trust: go vet; go test -count=1 ./...; go test -race -count=1 ./...; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/...; npm ci --prefix ui then npm test --prefix ui (57 tests); make ui then git status --porcelain empty. THREE REVIEW CONCLUSIONS required before approval. Architecture: the affected layers are internal/gitstore (a plain history question added, still ignorant of application schemas), internal/service (ordinary Git history added as a fourth distinction beside kernel refusal, application interpretation, durable state and live state) and ui/ (two screens); docs/reference/architecture.md is updated in this same head and its docs artifact is published here, so state whether the contract is preserved or changed. Security: the new POST /v0/landed is the one new trust boundary — the browser names commits and never the ref, the service resolves refs/heads/main then refs/heads/master itself, commit names are regex-validated before any git process starts, the batch is capped at LandingLimit, and a check that could not run renders as unknown rather than as a negative; examine those bounds and failure modes. Simplification: identify anything cuttable without weakening the conditions above. DEVIATIONS declared for your judgement, each with its reason in the commit message: POST /v0/landed is a new HTTP surface the note did not name, added because /v0/graph is a newest-80 window that would have reported b3bf3083 absent, which is the exact false negative the note's own post-mortem is about; ProfilePane is deleted because two screens leaves no room for a third pane; the commit-graph Railway drawing is absorbed rather than moved, so each of the report, verdict and merge stations carries its own commit on the rail row and no second picture survives; semanticActions is kept on spine rows because the #3923 case ends in ratifying a report and a screen must not name an action it cannot perform.","head":"c46445024fe159433